{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2337 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a8b5d683666676e9a4bca7e6b5f2e3c26528c5c7a0eb94e90a9ab8a81eafb1cc" :edb/db-before-t 2336 :edb/db-after-t 2337 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535649 50 #inst "2026-10-09T04:27:25.219Z" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092021 1100 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535649 false] [17592186092021 1100 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/901d3a22065b48a8076b9c9aae5563c770c36c9ad40e4063c0f739847e1cda98.png)" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092021 1145 "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I$:\n﻿﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}2 - λ & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}2 - λ & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(2 - λ)(2 - λ) - 4 \\cdot 3 &= 0 \\\\\n4 - 4λ + λ^{2} - 12 &= 0 \\\\\nλ^{2} - 4λ - 8 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535649 false] [17592186092021 1145 "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/0c6f9f860a1cf4d510f6c3d4d9c66b77496a354bb1e2cef1b69fd1178e4f15ab.png)\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4\\cdot 3 & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092022 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/5ca3e07cfbe9e5d4956b1eab4393601f2a78b0b067d17312e71cbac993e28a86.png)" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092022 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535649 false] [17592186092022 1145 "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 - λ & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(B - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}4 - λ & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(4 - λ)(4 - λ) - 0 \\cdot 0 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ - 4)^{2} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4$, which is a double root of the characteristic equation.\n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2$." 13194139535649 false] [17592186092022 1145 "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/fdbcc62870aefab6214b2f24f53e9bc5654e5386639d4bc328dff3769aff2b45.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation. \n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2.$" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092023 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/a1b88b7897649bb059cef39d40b2b052a13ac28282223b5688a1bce98296fb53.png)" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092023 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535649 false] [17592186092023 1145 "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I$:\n﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}10 - λ & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}10 - λ & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(10 - λ)(7 - λ) - 3 \\cdot 6 &= 0 \\\\\n70 - 7λ - 10λ + λ^{2} - 18 &= 0 \\\\\nλ^{2} - 17λ + 52 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= (17 ± \\sqrt{(-17)^{2} - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 52})/(2 \\cdot 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{17 ± \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{17 ± 9}{2} \\\\\n&= 13, 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4$." 13194139535649 false] [17592186092023 1145 "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/ca8f02e390e338b62956302ec45ea274ad73a51dafde3fe93b3d1e37dd663699.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-3\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ 70-7\\lambda -10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-17\\lambda +52 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{(-17)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =13,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4.$" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092024 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/603c59d43e3be000931e7279ac4d27be8aa92692f1528ec57ebd52172affa3cb.png)" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092024 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535649 false] [17592186092024 1145 "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/f91e4886c58db10f60fa666a870aed3c2f456b25e6afb560f857e9c36e81217c.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )-9\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues $\\lambda={\\color{red}3}$ and $\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}.$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/aa89b93c6fabd2f3dc7063c85e253ded7482018a5f1c6dadedc74964194c5754.png)\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092024 1145 "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I$:\n﻿﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}3 - λ & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3} - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}3 - λ & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3} - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(3 - λ)(-2\\sqrt{3} - λ) - 9 \\cdot 0 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ - 3)(λ + 2\\sqrt{3}) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues\n\n$$\n\\lambda={\\color{red}3}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!" 13194139535649 false] [17592186092176 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359170 13194139535649 true] [17592186092176 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359205 13194139535649 true] [17592186092176 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359226 13194139535649 true] [17592186092176 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359247 13194139535649 true] [17592186092177 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359198 13194139535649 true] [17592186092177 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359219 13194139535649 true] [17592186092177 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359233 13194139535649 true] [17592186092177 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359240 13194139535649 true] [17592186092178 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359212 13194139535649 true] [17592186092178 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359261 13194139535649 true] [17592186092178 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359268 13194139535649 true] [17592186092178 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359275 13194139535649 true] [17592186092179 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359177 13194139535649 true] [17592186092179 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359184 13194139535649 true] [17592186092179 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359191 13194139535649 true] [17592186092179 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359254 13194139535649 true] [17592186092462 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535649 true] [17592186092462 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535649 false] [17592186092462 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092462 1145 "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -\\sqrt{3})(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." 13194139535649 true] [17592186092636 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535649 true] [17592186092636 1100 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535649 false] [17592186092636 1100 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -6\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092636 1145 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ -8 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ -8 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )-(-8)\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ -12-2\\lambda +6\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092638 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535649 true] [17592186092638 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n\n$Q = \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535649 false] [17592186092638 1100 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535649 true] [17592186092638 1145 "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-6-\\lambda )(-10-\\lambda )-(-3)\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ 60+6\\lambda +10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+16\\lambda +66 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={16}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 66 \\\\  & =256-264 \\\\  & =-8 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions, and therefore, $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues." 13194139535649 true] [17592186359170 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359171 13194139535649 true] [17592186359170 1089 "q-106958" 13194139535649 true] [17592186359170 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535649 true] [17592186359170 1100 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535649 true] [17592186359170 1113 #uuid "800018b3-d1f0-57dc-9733-5d56dae63cca" 13194139535649 true] [17592186359170 1145 "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-0\\cdot (-1) & =0 \\\\ 5-5\\lambda -\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+0 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535649 true] [17592186359171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359172 13194139535649 true] [17592186359171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359173 13194139535649 true] [17592186359171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359174 13194139535649 true] [17592186359171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359175 13194139535649 true] [17592186359171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359176 13194139535649 true] [17592186359171 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535649 true] [17